                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Make a mess with plushies![/h1]\r\n\r\nPlush is a cheap puzzle physics sim where you play as the imaginary friend of a little girl that is determined to make you do her bidding. You are her slave! Err I mean it felt that way at times. She's mean. :(\r\n\r\nThe physics sometimes feels off and the toys will bounce away like crazy. I swear I dropped it in the same place three times and it went in different directions. You basically just end up guessing and get lucky or not.\r\n\r\nThe music puts me to sleep but this seems to be just me, cause slow music makes me Zzzzzzz. It may also be the fact that I'm staring at a bed the entire game.\r\n\r\nIt's just an ok game at best, I give this one a strong maybe vote. It's very cheap so can't really complain and it does what it says it does.\r\n\r\n[h2]6/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h2][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h2]",
